window.docContents[210].resolve({"/LindenstraussPolynomials/LemmaK/#mod-doc-LindenstraussPolynomials___LemmaK-1-0":{"contents":"An estimate for nonnegative polynomials \\(Lemma lem:K\\)\n\nFor every n\\ge1 there is K_n\\ge1 such that\n\\max_{0\\le t\\le1} r(t) \\le K_n\\int_0^1 r(t)\\,dt\nfor every real polynomial r of degree at most n that is nonnegative on [0,1].\n\nThe formal proof minimizes \\int_0^1|r| over the unit sphere of the coefficient space, which is compact; the article argues by contradiction with Vandermonde interpolation. Both prove the same statement.\n\n\n","context":"","header":"LindenstraussPolynomials.LemmaK","id":"/LindenstraussPolynomials/LemmaK/#mod-doc-LindenstraussPolynomials___LemmaK-1-0"}});